!! PhotoMap.in
!! Photolysis rates passed from TUV to ASP in SAM-ASP-TUV.
!!
!! Each line sets (or adds to) one ASP photolysis rate column, i.e. the
!! column number used for photolysis reactions in GasChemicalMechanism.in
!! ("; 0.; N.") and in PhotoRates.in, from one TUV photolysis reaction:
!!
!!     ASP column ; scale factor ; TUV reaction label
!!
!! The label must match TUV's label exactly (as listed in TUV's input file
!! SRC_TUV/TUV/INPUTS/samasp, without the leading T/F and number), and that
!! reaction must be switched on (T) there. Lines with the same column are
!! summed. A column used by the mechanism with no line here, an unknown
!! label, or a column outside PhotoRates.in stops the run at start-up.
!!
!! Columns 49-51 have no TUV reaction; they are set from TUV rates for
!! similar species with constant ratios:
!!   49 = 0.33 x J(propanal)    (butanal channel 1 and other aldehydes)
!!   50 = 0.16 x J(propanal)    (butanal channel 2)
!!   51 = 100  x J(methacrolein) (HPALD1, HPALD2)
!!
  1 ; 1.0  ; O2 -> O + O
  2 ; 1.0  ; O3 -> O2 + O(1D)
  3 ; 1.0  ; O3 -> O2 + O(3P)
  4 ; 1.0  ; HO2 -> OH + O
  5 ; 1.0  ; H2O2 -> 2 OH
  6 ; 1.0  ; NO2 -> NO + O(3P)
  7 ; 1.0  ; NO3 -> NO + O2
  8 ; 1.0  ; NO3 -> NO2 + O(3P)
  9 ; 1.0  ; N2O5 -> NO3 + NO + O(3P)
 10 ; 1.0  ; N2O5 -> NO3 + NO2
 11 ; 1.0  ; N2O -> N2 + O(1D)
 12 ; 1.0  ; HNO2 -> OH + NO
 13 ; 1.0  ; HNO3 -> OH + NO2
 14 ; 1.0  ; HNO4 -> HO2 + NO2
 15 ; 1.0  ; NO3-(aq) -> NO2(aq) + O-
 16 ; 1.0  ; NO3-(aq) -> NO2-(aq) + O(3P)
 17 ; 1.0  ; CH2O -> H + HCO
 18 ; 1.0  ; CH2O -> H2 + CO
 19 ; 1.0  ; CH3CHO -> CH3 + HCO
 20 ; 1.0  ; CH3CHO -> CH4 + CO
 21 ; 1.0  ; CH3CHO -> CH3CO + H
 22 ; 1.0  ; C2H5CHO -> C2H5 + HCO
 23 ; 1.0  ; HOCH2CHO -> CH2OH + HCO
 23 ; 1.0  ; HOCH2CHO -> CH3OH + CO
 23 ; 1.0  ; HOCH2CHO -> CH2CHO + OH
 24 ; 1.0  ; CH2=CHCHO -> Products
 25 ; 1.0  ; CH2=C(CH3)CHO -> Products
 26 ; 1.0  ; CH3COCH3 -> CH3CO + CH3
 27 ; 1.0  ; CH3COCH=CH2 -> Products
 28 ; 1.0  ; CH3COCH2CH3 -> CH3CO + CH2CH3
 29 ; 1.0  ; CH2(OH)COCH3 -> CH3CO + CH2(OH)
 30 ; 1.0  ; CH2(OH)COCH3 -> CH2(OH)CO + CH3
 31 ; 1.0  ; CH3OOH -> CH3O + OH
 32 ; 1.0  ; HOCH2OOH -> HOCH2O. + OH
 33 ; 1.0  ; CH3CO(OOH) -> Products
 34 ; 1.0  ; CH3ONO2 -> CH3O + NO2
 35 ; 1.0  ; CH3CH2ONO2 -> CH3CH2O + NO2
 36 ; 1.0  ; CH3CHONO2CH3 -> CH3CHOCH3 + NO2
 37 ; 1.0  ; CH2(OH)CH2(ONO2) -> CH2(OH)CH2(O.) + NO2
 38 ; 1.0  ; CH3COCH2(ONO2) -> CH3COCH2(O.) + NO2
 39 ; 1.0  ; C(CH3)3(ONO2) -> C(CH3)3(O.) + NO2
 40 ; 1.0  ; CH3CO(OONO2) -> CH3CO(OO) + NO2
 41 ; 1.0  ; CH3CO(OONO2) -> CH3CO(O) + NO3
 42 ; 1.0  ; CH3CH2CO(OONO2) -> CH3CH2CO(OO) + NO2
 43 ; 1.0  ; CH3CH2CO(OONO2) -> CH3CH2CO(O) + NO3
 44 ; 1.0  ; CHOCHO -> HCO + HCO
 45 ; 1.0  ; CHOCHO -> CH2O + CO
 46 ; 1.0  ; CH3COCHO -> CH3CO + HCO
 47 ; 1.0  ; CH3COCOCH3 -> Products
 48 ; 1.0  ; CH3COCO(OH) -> Products
 49 ; 0.33 ; C2H5CHO -> C2H5 + HCO
 50 ; 0.16 ; C2H5CHO -> C2H5 + HCO
 51 ; 100. ; CH2=C(CH3)CHO -> Products
